Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: a renewed radio's Channel Preference Query and policy request do not wait for configured siblings

0234 let a renewed radio past the AP Capability Query; it then waited one step later. In
channel_query_pending the controller sends the agent's Channel Preference Query only when
every radio of the agent is there, and from the agent's first radio; in set_policy_pending
it sends the Multi-AP Policy Config from the agent's first radio. When only one radio is
renewed (its em_config timed out, it was marked misconfigured and AutoConfig Renew re-ran WSC
for it alone) its siblings stay configured: the query waited for them, or the first radio,
configured and executing nothing, sent no request. The renewed radio waited until its
em_config timed out ("Canceling cmd: em_config because time limit exceeded"), was renewed
and waited again, for ever (rdk-1004, 6 October 2026: the wired extender's 2.4 GHz radio
renewed 43 times in 22 minutes, its 5 GHz radio with it; while it cycled it refused
candidate queries with Error_Not_Ready, the optimizer's snapshot stayed incomplete and the
rooms did not converge).

As in 0233 and 0234: only a sibling still onboarding (before channel_query_pending) holds
the query, and the radio that sends the query, or the policy request, is elected among the
radios waiting for it. The report and the ACK still move every radio that waits.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/em/channel/em_channel.cpp
+++ b/src/em/channel/em_channel.cpp
@@ -2509,17 +2509,25 @@
                 std::vector<em_t *> em_radios;
                 dm_easy_mesh_t *dm = get_data_model();
                 get_mgr()->get_all_em_for_al_mac(dm->get_agent_al_interface_mac(), em_radios);
+                em_t *query_em = NULL;
                 for (auto &em : em_radios) {
-                    if (em->get_state() != em_state_ctrl_channel_query_pending) {
-                        em_util_dbg_print(EM_CONF, "radio %s is not in channel query pending state, ignoring",
-                            util::mac_to_string(em->get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str());
+                    // Only a sibling still onboarding (before this query) holds it. One
+                    // already past it, because it finished earlier and only this radio was
+                    // renewed, must not: waiting for it times this radio's em_config out,
+                    // renews it and waits again, for ever.
+                    if (em->get_state() < em_state_ctrl_channel_query_pending) {
+                        em_util_dbg_print(EM_CONF, "radio %s is in state:%d, before the Channel Preference query, ignoring",
+                            util::mac_to_string(em->get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str(), em->get_state());
                         em_radios.clear();
                         return;
                     }
+                    // The radio that sends the query is elected among the radios waiting
+                    // for it: a sibling already past it may be executing another command.
+                    if ((query_em == NULL) && (em->get_state() == em_state_ctrl_channel_query_pending)) {
+                        query_em = em;
+                    }
                 }
-                // If all radios are in Channel pref query pending state, send channel pref query on one of them, 
-                // ignore sending channel query query on other radios
-                if (this == em_radios.front()){
+                if (this == query_em){
                     em_printfout("Sending the Channel pref query message to agent al_mac:%s on radio: %s",
